{
  "title": "QUADRATICS,\n(THE DISCRIMINANT)",
  "objective": "LO: I can use the discriminant to determine the number and nature of roots of a quadratic equation.",
  "send_mode": false,
  "info_boxes": {
    "key_terms": {
      "id": "key_terms",
      "title": "What is the discriminant?",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The <span class=\"ul-b\">discriminant</span> of ax&sup2; + bx + c = 0 is <span class=\"ul-k\">b&sup2; &minus; 4ac</span>. It tells us how many real roots (solutions) the quadratic has."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "<span class=\"rb\">Key results:</span> If b&sup2; &minus; 4ac &gt; 0: two distinct real roots. If = 0: one repeated root. If &lt; 0: no real roots."
        }
      ]
    },
    "what_we_learn": {
      "id": "what_we_learn",
      "title": "Quick examples",
      "examples": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "expr": "x&sup2; + 5x + 6: b&sup2;&minus;4ac = 25&minus;24 = 1 &gt; 0, two roots",
          "desc": "positive discriminant"
        },
        {
          "correct": true,
          "expr": "x&sup2; &minus; 6x + 9: b&sup2;&minus;4ac = 36&minus;36 = 0, one root",
          "desc": "zero discriminant"
        },
        {
          "correct": true,
          "expr": "x&sup2; + x + 1: b&sup2;&minus;4ac = 1&minus;4 = &minus;3 &lt; 0, no real roots",
          "desc": "negative discriminant"
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "expr": "Discriminant = b&sup2; + 4ac",
          "desc": "must be b&sup2; MINUS 4ac"
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "expr": "b&sup2; &minus; 4ac &lt; 0 means two real roots",
          "desc": "negative means no real roots"
        }
      ]
    },
    "key_idea": {
      "id": "key_idea",
      "title": "Key idea",
      "text": "The discriminant b&sup2; &minus; 4ac determines the nature of roots: positive = 2 roots, zero = 1, negative = none.",
      "equation": "&Delta; = <span class=\"ov\">b&sup2;</span> &minus; <span class=\"ovr\">4ac</span>",
      "caption": "&Delta; &gt; 0: two roots; &Delta; = 0: one root; &Delta; &lt; 0: no real roots"
    }
  },
  "modelled_examples": [
    {
      "id": "ex1",
      "card_color": "#1F5FA6",
      "card_bg": "#EEF3FF",
      "label": "Example 1 &ndash; two real roots",
      "question": "Find the discriminant of x&sup2; + 3x &minus; 10 = 0 and state the number of roots.",
      "steps": [
        "a = 1, b = 3, c = &minus;10",
        "&Delta; = 3&sup2; &minus; 4(1)(&minus;10) = 9 + 40 = 49",
        "&Delta; = 49 &gt; 0, so two distinct real roots"
      ],
      "answer": "Two distinct real roots",
      "explanation": "Since 49 is a perfect square, the roots will be rational."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex2",
      "card_color": "#1F5FA6",
      "card_bg": "#EEF3FF",
      "label": "Example 2 &ndash; repeated root",
      "question": "Find the discriminant of x&sup2; &minus; 8x + 16 = 0.",
      "steps": [
        "a = 1, b = &minus;8, c = 16",
        "&Delta; = (&minus;8)&sup2; &minus; 4(1)(16) = 64 &minus; 64 = 0",
        "&Delta; = 0, so one repeated root"
      ],
      "answer": "One repeated root",
      "explanation": "The quadratic is a perfect square: (x &minus; 4)&sup2; = 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex3",
      "card_color": "#CC0000",
      "card_bg": "#FFF0F0",
      "label": "Example 3 &ndash; no real roots",
      "question": "Show that 2x&sup2; + x + 3 = 0 has no real roots.",
      "steps": [
        "a = 2, b = 1, c = 3",
        "&Delta; = 1&sup2; &minus; 4(2)(3) = 1 &minus; 24 = &minus;23",
        "&Delta; = &minus;23 &lt; 0, so no real roots"
      ],
      "answer": "No real roots",
      "explanation": "A negative discriminant means the parabola does not cross the x-axis."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex4",
      "card_color": "#1E7D2E",
      "card_bg": "#EDFAEE",
      "label": "Example 4 &ndash; finding k for equal roots",
      "question": "Find k if x&sup2; + kx + 9 = 0 has equal roots.",
      "steps": [
        "For equal roots: &Delta; = 0",
        "k&sup2; &minus; 4(1)(9) = 0 &rArr; k&sup2; = 36",
        "k = &plusmn;6"
      ],
      "answer": "k = 6 or k = &minus;6",
      "explanation": "Set the discriminant to zero and solve for the parameter."
    }
  ],
